    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_140",
        "cnm_276"
      ],
      "explanation": "A right triangle with a \\(30^\\circ\\) angle gives a geometric way to find the sine. Let its hypotenuse have length \\(h>0\\). The side opposite \\(30^\\circ\\) has length \\(h/2\\), so the definition of sine gives\n\\[\n\\sin30^\\circ=\\frac{h/2}{h}=\\frac12.\n\\]",
      "id": "m2",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_h060_q2#m2",
      "title": "Use a right-triangle side ratio"
    }
